{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/839674-nosferatu-bloodline-the-moerus","id":839674,"title":"Nosferatu Bloodline: the Moerus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-29T21:26:25-08:00","id":839674,"title":"Nosferatu Bloodline: the Moerus","content":"Below is a bloodline I first made a few years ago after reading Requiem for Rome and being really taken with its portrayal of the Nosferatu. I was also a big Legion of the Dead fan, doubly so when I found out they became ruthless mercenaries after the Camarilla fell apart. Both of those went into the design for this one, carrying some of that forward into modern days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B89Dq1vELvMNbnVVaklQZUFGRjQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B89Dq1vELvMNbnVVaklQZUFGRjQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B89Dq1vELvMNbnVVaklQZUFGRjQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B89Dq1vELvMNbnVVaklQZUFGRjQ/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:54:15-08:00","id":840216,"title":"","content":"I liked the Moerus when you first came up with them, and I like them now. I'm fond of the reasons behind their founding and their drive for perpetuating tradition. They don't have a bloodline Gift, so maybe they could use one that played into familial loyalty or was based on their namelessness as the Brothers Worm? Also of note: the progression and adaptation of their culture to the current era. Details like that give it a very interesting sense of historical malleability and progress in relation to their identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:57:15-08:00","id":840219,"title":"","content":"I knew I forgot something. Bloodline Gifts.<br /> <br /> Those weren't a thing back when I first came up with them, so I'm really a little at a loss to figure out what would be appropriate for them on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank